{
  "title": "Imperfect and future tenses",
  "note": "The imperfect shows ongoing or repeated past action with -ba-: amabam, I was loving or used to love; monebam, regebam, audiebam. The future of the first and second conjugations uses -bo, -bis, -bit: amabo, I will love. The third and fourth use -am, -es, -et: regam, reges, reget; audiam, audies, audiet. Sum has eram (I was) and ero (I will be).",
  "src": {
    "t": "Allen and Greenough, Tenses",
    "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/grammar/latin/tenses"
  },
